      "raw_text": "To find the number of men who can stay upright on the wave, we need to break the problem down into logical steps based on the information provided.\n\n**Step 1: Determine the total number of riders who can stay upright.**\nThe problem states that there are 100 riders in total.\nIt also states that when a wave over 30 feet arrives, only 25% of the riders can stay upright.\nWe calculate 25% of 100:\n$$100 \\times 0.25 = 25$$\nSo, 25 riders can stay upright.\n\n**Step 2: Determine the number of women among the riders who stay upright.**\nThe problem states that of the riders who stay upright (the 25 identified in Step 1), 60% are women.\nWe calculate 60% of 25:\n$$25 \\times 0.60 = 15$$\nSo, 15 of the riders who stayed upright are women.\n\n**Step 3: Determine the number of men among the riders who stay upright.**\nThe group of riders who stay upright consists entirely of men and women. We know there are 25 people in this group and 15 of them are women. To find the number of men, we subtract the number of women from the total number of upright riders:\n$$25 - 15 = 10$$\n\nTherefore, 10 men can stay upright on the wave.\n\n#### 10<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To find the number of men who can stay upright on the wave, we need to break the problem down into logical steps based on the information provided.\n\n**Step 1: Determine the total number of riders who can stay upright.**\nThe problem states that there are 100 riders in total.\nIt also states that when a wave over 30 feet arrives, only 25% of the riders can stay upright.\nWe calculate 25% of 100:\n$$100 \\times 0.25 = 25$$\nSo, 25 riders can stay upright.\n\n**Step 2: Determine the number of women among the riders who stay upright.**\nThe problem states that of the riders who stay upright (the 25 identified in Step 1), 60% are women.\nWe calculate 60% of 25:\n$$25 \\times 0.60 = 15$$\nSo, 15 of the riders who stayed upright are women.\n\n**Step 3: Determine the number of men among the riders who stay upright.**\nThe group of riders who stay upright consists entirely of men and women. We know there are 25 people in this group and 15 of them are women. To find the number of men, we subtract the number of women from the total number of upright riders:\n$$25 - 15 = 10$$\n\nTherefore, 10 men can stay upright on the wave.\n\n#### 10",
      "input_sha256": "c79c63dca99626ffb243a43597c887c69c2edecd3bcb517d7997e5a73dbfdcb8",
      "parsed_answer": "10",
      "correct": true
    }
